{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan revised after review run 1 (PASS with advisories). Folded in: (1) the pid <= 0 guard, since OpenProcess returns 87 for pid 0; (2) explicit ctypes argtypes/restype, with the last error read through use_last_error plus get_last_error, both injectable; (3) a stop() helper that waits for the real interpreter pid to read dead before any not-running assertion; (4) all 4 Popen(['true']) dead-pid copies, including test_lock_age_ceiling and test_lock_container_recreate, routed through a shared dead_pid(); (5) the product consumers in compact_trigger named; (6) AC1 evidence taken from the first scheduled main run after merge, with the tmp-branch dispatch kept as pre-merge validation. AC block unchanged."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795257360050282001,"uuid":"31a5a463-4b7a-4f45-b5e0-6cd77d6b88a8"}